## 🚫 Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### Don't Use Stringly-Typed Code

```swift
// ❌ Bad: String-based keys
let name = userInfo["name"] as? String

// ✅ Good: Type-safe keys
struct UserInfo {
    let name: String
}
```

### Don't Use Force Unwrapping

```swift
// ❌ Bad: Force unwrapping
let country = countries.first!

// ✅ Good: Safe unwrapping
guard let country = countries.first else { return }
```

### Don't Ignore Errors

```swift
// ❌ Bad: Silent failures
try? fetchCountries()

// ✅ Good: Handle errors
do {
    try await fetchCountries()
} catch {
    logger.error("Failed to fetch: \(error)")
}
```

### Don't Use Massive View Controllers/ViewModels

```swift
// ❌ Bad: 1000+ line ViewModels
// ✅ Good: Break into smaller, focused components
```

